{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "1152f2c5-ffc4-8690-9f4b-30f7da934ebd",
  "created_at": "2026-02-23T11:12:43-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Nora Cullen",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:08:42-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:08:45-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi Kevin, Nora Cullen. I'm calling about a flooded low spot at the end of my block. It's been sitting there since the storm and it's not draining."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:08:55-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, the storm over the weekend, the nor'easter?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:08:59-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, last weekend's, Saturday into Sunday. It's Monday now and that water is still there. It's easily a foot deep, maybe a little more at the middle."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:09:09-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A foot, wow. Alright, let me write that down. Low spot, about a foot of water, still standing from the weekend. Is it a road, a corner, what are we looking at?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:09:20-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's the dip at the end of the street where it meets the cross street. Water pools right across both lanes. Cars are slowing to a crawl going through it, some of them are sitting there deciding whether to chance it. I watched a guy in a sedan almost stall."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:09:37-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that's not great. Do you know if there's a storm drain right there, or is it just the low spot?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:09:45-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a grate at the curb, but it's got to be clogged or backed up, because nothing's moving. This is not the first time either. Every decent storm it does this and then it just sits."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:09:58-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. Every storm, same spot. And what's the street name? I'll need the closest address or cross street too."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:10:06-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, I'd rather not give the house, it's not about my house. It's the corner at the end of the block, you can't miss it, it looks like a pond. Can I give you the cross street instead?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:10:19-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, the cross street works, and I can pin it from that. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:10:25-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, hang on, I'm looking out the window. [pause] Sorry, my head's all over the place. I've got to be at work, I start my housekeeping shift at the hotel in forty minutes, so I've got to leave soon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:10:39-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, we'll be quick. Take your time on the cross street, I've got it open on the map."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:10:46-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's where Bellevue Avenue runs into the end of my street, down by the little park. That corner."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:10:53-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Bellevue end, near the park. That's enough for me to find it. Do you want a callback number on this?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:11:01-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, it's 401-555-0167. That's the landline here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:11:04-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great, 401-555-0167. So what I'll do is put this in as a drainage request for Public Works, standing water, about a foot, affecting traffic."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:11:13-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. And that's what I'm asking, will there actually be a work order opened? And for what date? Because I don't want to hear someone will look at it and then it's still a lake on Friday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:11:26-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I'm opening the work order while we're talking. Crews are slammed after a storm like this, so I'd say they'll get out there in the next couple of days, probably Tuesday or Wednesday, and they'll check that drain first."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:11:40-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Tuesday or Wednesday. Okay. If it's a clogged grate that's a quick fix, honestly. It's not like they need to dig up the road."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:11:49-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, I'll note that you think it's the grate. If it's blocked they can usually clear it fast. If it turns out to be something bigger, the pipe, it'll go to a different list and someone will let you know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:12:03-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine. Can you give me the work order number so I can reference it if I have to call back?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:12:10-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, hold on one second. [pause] Okay, it's saved, and it's showing up on my screen as request number four-four-one-seven."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:12:17-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-four-one-seven. Got it. I'll call Wednesday afternoon if it's not done."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:12:22-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That works. And if it gets worse, or somebody gets stuck in it, call right back and say so, because then it's a safety issue and it moves up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:12:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks, Kevin. I've got to run, I'll be late."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:12:36-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No worries, drive safe, and watch that puddle on your way out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:12:41-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, I will. Bye."
    }
  ],
